    "description": "<p>Under the sharp contraction and joining results specified in the paper, we prove linear stability of binary-information contraction on every compact amplitude and correlation rectangle, uniformly over finite cube dimensions. For information psi(a) tending to zero, the constant grows at most as a to the power -4, and this exponent is necessary. The statements apply to arbitrary [-1,1]-valued kernels, without a mean restriction or a pointwise interior margin. We also strengthen the entropy-production inequality D(u) &gt;= F(I(u)) by an absolute positive multiple of (E u) squared times I(u) squared. The proof combines strict Gaussian contraction, a compactness argument for joining laws, and estimates retaining the entropy of rare endpoint values.</p>",
    "references": [
      {
        "reference": "W. Beckner, Inequalities in Fourier analysis, Annals of Mathematics 102 (1975), 159–182."
      },
      {
        "reference": "A. Bonami, Étude des coefficients de Fourier des fonctions de Lp (G), Annales de l'Institut Fourier 20 (1970), no. 2, 335–402."
      },
      {
        "reference": "Z. Chen, A. Gohari, and C. Nair, A differential equation approach to the most-informative Boolean function conjecture, arXiv:2502.10019v2, 2026."
      },
      {
        "reference": "Z. Chen, A. Gohari, A. Javanmard, H. Lin, V. Mirrokni, C. Nair, and D. P. Woodruff, A proof of the most informative Boolean function conjecture, arXiv:2609.24931v2, 2026."
      },
      {
        "reference": "S. Heilman and A. Tarter, Three candidate plurality is stablest for small correlations, Forum of Mathematics, Sigma 9 (2021), e65. doi:10.1017/fms.2021.56. Lemma numbers refer to arXiv:2011.05583v2."
      },
      {
        "reference": "V. K. Ky and T. Tran, Stability of the Courtade–Kumar inequality, arXiv:2609.31797, 2026."
      },
      {
        "reference": "E. Mossel and J. Neeman, Robust optimality of Gaussian noise stability, arXiv:1210.4126v3, 2013, Theorem 1.1 and Section 2 (Borell's two-set inequality)."
      },
